# SeDoc CODEOWNERS
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rules:
# - Last matching pattern wins.
# - Patterns starting with `/` are anchored to repo root.
# - Today @ezcobar owns everything. As the team grows, replace the per-area
#   owners below — the layout is here so future per-service tech leads can
#   slot in without restructuring the file.
# - The /docs/security/ block is the security-lead override and must always
#   require security-lead review, even if a service lead owns the rest of
#   their service.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — catch-all for anything not matched below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go services (services/*)
# Each line is a placeholder for the eventual service tech lead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/services/audit/                        @ezcobar
/services/auth/                         @ezcobar
/services/billing/                      @ezcobar
/services/collaboration/                @ezcobar
/services/connector/                    @ezcobar
/services/document/                     @ezcobar
/services/graphql-gateway/              @ezcobar
/services/intelligence/                 @ezcobar
/services/mcp-server/                   @ezcobar
/services/notification/                 @ezcobar
/services/policy/                       @ezcobar
/services/preview/                      @ezcobar
/services/search/                       @ezcobar
/services/signature/                    @ezcobar
/services/signature-signer/             @ezcobar
/services/storage/                      @ezcobar
/services/workflow/                     @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared libraries and contracts — changes here ripple across every service,
# so they should always need an extra reviewer once a second owner exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/pkg/                                   @ezcobar
/proto/                                 @ezcobar
/cmd/                                   @ezcobar
/go.work                                @ezcobar
/go.work.sum                            @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend, mobile, addins, extension
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/web/                                   @ezcobar
/mobile/                                @ezcobar
/addins/                                @ezcobar
/extension/                             @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build, deploy, ops, CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Makefile                               @ezcobar
/docker-compose*.yml                    @ezcobar
/deploy/                                @ezcobar
/ops/                                   @ezcobar
/.github/                               @ezcobar
/.github/workflows/                     @ezcobar
/scripts/                               @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/                                  @ezcobar
/docs/adr/                              @ezcobar
/CHANGELOG.md                           @ezcobar
/README.md                              @ezcobar
/SETUP.md                               @ezcobar
/CLAUDE.md                              @ezcobar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security — explicit override. Anything under here requires the security
# lead, regardless of which service it appears to live in. This is the line
